18" :question/math-academy-id "q-48872" :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}+1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{2}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}+1} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}}{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}}{1+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{1+0} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-48872/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32cbf366-20bd-5a52-a14f-83add698bf07"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48872"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339426/field-1/5d34995cddd0166b343cae457ee45643c04c739e08758db1204c66c5ee04158e" :answer/id #uuid "fcbd9826-5bdd-5cd8-a2f1-e2ccfd185fab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339426/field-1/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" :answer/id #uuid "df03a4ca-7222-5b90-ab10-7896e65d7dd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339426/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa9fc928-6a48-5a69-891b-6361fb00fd55" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-339426/field-1/5d34995cddd0166b343cae457ee45643c04c739e08758db1204c66c5ee04158e" :answer-field/choices ["q-339426/field-1/5d34995cddd0166b343cae457ee45643c04c739e08758db1204c66c5ee04158e" "q-339426/field-1/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339426" :question/id #uuid "19f08822-38c8-5644-ae87-60cc80530130" :question/math-academy-id "q-339426" :question/problem "Given that ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{3-x-8{x}^{2}}{k\\,{x}^{2}+7x-4}=\\frac{2}{5},$  what is the value of $k?$\n\n$k=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{2}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{3-x-8{x}^{2}}{k\\,{x}^{2}+7x-4} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{8{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}})}{(\\frac{k{x}^{2}}{\\,{x}^{2}}+\\frac{7x}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{x}-8)}{(k+\\frac{7}{x}-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-0-8}{k+0-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8}{k} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{8}{k} & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ 2k & =-40 \\\\ k & =-20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-339426/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32cbf366-20bd-5a52-a14f-83add698bf07"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339426"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48842/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "09724855-4426-53b4-be0d-7b66abcd56a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48842/selection/2aef90071200a7bc65baa2d03f49803233ca7b2dc16865265136281ee914878b" :answer/id #uuid "496df943-5038-5541-9890-1d107235d50f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48842/selection/3224ab5f6f5fb64621a714f7654c4df06661a69e7edb8f5993dcef1e46ce3dea" :answer/id #uuid "ce9f4d3a-fc28-52b6-9eb0-2377767a8822" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48842/selection/d427b944e26709d5f365fc6b5711be004a0a3509f614cbfd4943dc70d3f6d84e" :answer/id #uuid "e489e715-a582-5444-b867-8dd9214e0e23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48842/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer/id #uuid "22f83812-718c-5f5c-8964-b18c0f8ef05c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48842/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fec2c85a-902a-580e-9eed-6a94b46d3c10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48842/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer-field/choices ["q-48842/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" "q-48842/selection/2aef90071200a7bc65baa2d03f49803233ca7b2dc16865265136281ee914878b" "q-48842/selection/3224ab5f6f5fb64621a714f7654c4df06661a69e7edb8f5993dcef1e46ce3dea" "q-48842/selection/d427b944e26709d5f365fc6b5711be004a0a3509f614cbfd4943dc70d3f6d84e" "q-48842/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48842" :question/id #uuid "d2725764-090f-55c8-a8ae-6f44078e0955" :question/math-academy-id "q-48842" :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{|6x-2|}{8x+5}=$" :question/worked-solution "For large positive values of $x,$ we have $|6x-2|=6x-2.$ Consequently, for $x\\to \\infty ,$ we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{|6x-2|}{8x+5}={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{6x-2}{8x+5}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{1}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{6x-2}{8x+5} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{6x}{x}-\\frac{2}{x})}{(\\frac{8x}{x}+\\frac{5}{x})} \\\\  & {lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(6-\\frac{2}{x})}{(8+\\frac{5}{x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-0}{8-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-48842/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32cbf366-20bd-5a52-a14f-83add698bf07"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48842"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48878/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "da171a55-46a5-570f-9b47-35c45d5ed257" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48878/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "97bff7cd-f222-5465-a362-a5f28d34a44f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48878/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "78e64852-3529-5914-973b-88cafa206ae4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48878/selection/edc901e84f0cdd5174afd49105ac3883566ea0e1e057217fb66083a56cc119ba" :answer/id #uuid "04a341e6-9e92-5d36-83bf-00989e140002" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48878/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "531f5633-6876-59d5-938f-09bb300f3186" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48878/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e5de6d13-5667-5cd8-a33e-a624a9d21207" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48878/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-48878/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-48878/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-48878/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-48878/selection/edc901e84f0cdd5174afd49105ac3883566ea0e1e057217fb66083a56cc119ba" "q-48878/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48878" :question/id #uuid "e48eb8c6-5d80-5eaa-9e9b-a82784e79ed8" :question/math-academy-id "q-48878" :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{|10x+3|}{6-5x}.$" :question/worked-solution "For large positive values of $x,$ we have $|10x+3|=10x+3.$ Consequently, for $x\\to \\infty ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{|10x+3|}{6-5x}=\\frac{10x+3}{6-5x}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{1}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{10x+3}{6-5x} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{10x}{x}+\\frac{3}{x})}{(\\frac{6}{x}-\\frac{5x}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(10+\\frac{3}{x})}{(\\frac{6}{x}-5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{10+0}{0-5} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-48878/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32cbf366-20bd-5a52-a14f-83add698bf07"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48878"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-3761"] :question/problem "Calculate ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{{x}^{4}-6}{{x}^{2}-x+2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{2}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{{x}^{4}-6}{{x}^{2}-x+2} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}})}{(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{({x}^{2}-\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}})}{(1-\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{({x}^{2}-0)}{(1-0+0)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,{x}^{2} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-339623/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "2a276290-ab0d-52b1-8807-4a9062f36d49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186275175 :answer-field/choices ["q-339623/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48717/selection/763a7c0b26f15df25c2db2d8ac42125e806c2e4b56e4f070b4566eba7e05dfff" :answer/id #uuid "891c10cf-3975-5d88-9192-f7f0de580a68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48717/selection/8b126ddfc3c4ba99c0bf8461003a3883177c32770aa009751d1bd45377619b2e" :answer/id #uuid "ed7e50b5-8e45-5f22-b8dd-647021d2934a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48717/selection/96efe327aa5df1953454aa8a0acb24299d8e2e2f538b2a5f40d98e7332b886b7" :answer/id #uuid "aaefbbb6-6fac-5fcc-bfd0-280001bcfcc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48717/selection/b4433cc3a1cf5e75fc9a785442bb7c0d16a914e01f6e6fe624ef0ea36d614fe6" :answer/id #uuid "1a9dd1d9-7ab5-5a9f-90f5-c307b35841d9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No horizontal asymptote" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48717/selection/25eb914fe9ac4d670cc8b64d7e8deee9c4123c32ede90f0fd11dc435564dd91d" :answer/id #uuid "57058574-7d70-5dd5-830b-c0559e3c6613" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48717/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b52d0826-ee50-53c5-ab1c-fa899c70ab44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48717/selection/763a7c0b26f15df25c2db2d8ac42125e806c2e4b56e4f070b4566eba7e05dfff" :answer-field/choices ["q-48717/selection/763a7c0b26f15df25c2db2d8ac42125e806c2e4b56e4f070b4566eba7e05dfff" "q-48717/selection/8b126ddfc3c4ba99c0bf8461003a3883177c32770aa009751d1bd45377619b2e" "q-48717/selection/96efe327aa5df1953454aa8a0acb24299d8e2e2f538b2a5f40d98e7332b886b7" "q-48717/selection/b4433cc3a1cf5e75fc9a785442bb7c0d16a914e01f6e6fe624ef0ea36d614fe6" "q-48717/selection/25eb914fe9ac4d670cc8b64d7e8deee9c4123c32ede90f0fd11dc435564dd91d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48717" :question/id #uuid "83afe3ca-ce48-5376-ba62-ad4d799e50bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-48717" :question/problem "What is the horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x)$ for $x<0$ with $f(x)=\\frac{|3x+6|}{x-4}?$" :question/worked-solution "For large negative values of $x,$ we have $|3x+6|=-(3x+6).$ Consequently, for $x\\to -\\infty ,$ we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{|3x+6|}{x-4}={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{-(3x+6)}{x-4}.\n$$\n\nThe horizontal asymptote for $x<0$ is $y={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is $x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{-(3x+6)}{x-4} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{-(\\frac{3x}{x}+\\frac{6}{x})}{(\\frac{x}{x}-\\frac{4}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{-(3+\\frac{6}{x})}{(1-\\frac{4}{x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(3+0)}{1-0} \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y=-3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-48717/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee15db10-b92c-5f48-8983-e602068c7e08"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48717"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-35829/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "01612fcc-c163-55eb-bd5c-be51e0fde1d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35829/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" :answer/id #uuid "fc18ba81-9a18-50c6-bd73-8a69f761e55d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35829/selection/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" :answer/id #uuid "1a058134-38f6-565d-b2a3-4a284546cca6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35829/selection/d278d4936eb1c69dc660a77f5f1c7b1eb5b4a4db4aee8a8ad2dc52aa3f827f2e" :answer/id #uuid "54725c8f-1119-598a-a096-27128790e6c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35829/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" :answer/id #uuid "dcc0c635-a4a1-5f47-adea-6dd1a54780c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35829/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "af43eb97-41d2-55c2-86db-fccc974e1e51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-35829/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" :answer-field/choices ["q-35829/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-35829/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" "q-35829/selection/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" "q-35829/selection/d278d4936eb1c69dc660a77f5f1c7b1eb5b4a4db4aee8a8ad2dc52aa3f827f2e" "q-35829/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-35829" :question/id #uuid "dfebc30a-ea33-5139-a1fd-71dc23f9282b" :question/math-academy-id "q-35829" :question/problem "Given that the horizontal asymptote of the function $f(x)=\\frac{5{x}^{2}-6}{c{x}^{2}+32x+8}$ is $y=\\frac{1}{4},$ find the value of $c.$" :question/worked-solution "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{2}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{5{x}^{2}-6}{c{x}^{2}+32x+8} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}})}{(\\frac{c{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{32x}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{8}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(5-\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}})}{(c+\\frac{32}{x}+\\frac{8}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-0}{c+0+0} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{c}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{c} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ c & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-35829/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee15db10-b92c-5f48-8983-e602068c7e08"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-35829"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-302242/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "87d01e32-49c1-59bc-b6e4-5333dcefcddc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-302242/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a793526-c408-5e79-a943-5c9ae00c391c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-302242/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer-field/choices ["q-302242/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-302242" :question/id #uuid "9f9b3b79-6712-5d2b-9420-7d4b4caf5430" :question/math-academy-id "q-302242" :question/problem "Given that the horizontal asymptote of the function $f(x)=\\frac{18{x}^{4}+5x}{c{x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}}$ is $y=\\frac{3}{2},$ find the value of $c.$\n\n$c=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{4}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{18{x}^{4}+5x}{c{x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{18{x}^{4}}{{x}^{4}}+\\frac{5x}{{x}^{4}})}{(\\frac{c{x}^{4}}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{{x}^{4}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(18+\\frac{5}{{x}^{3}})}{(c-\\frac{2}{x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{18+0}{c-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{c}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{18}{c} & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 36 & =3c \\\\ c & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-302242/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee15db10-b92c-5f48-8983-e602068c7e08"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-302242"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-35763"] :question/problem "Find the horizontal asymptote of the function $f(x)=\\frac{2x+5}{2{x}^{3}+2x+6}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-35836/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "1a60afa0-87a8-563c-947c-81930061bf2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35836/selection/e53026d2e72b5